# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# irabelle-stack — keep per-client configuration, secrets and generated
# runtime state OUT of git, so that:
#   * no credential ever reaches the repository, and
#   * `git status` stays clean on every client after the stack has been run.
#
# Patterns are written to cover future stacks too (`**/`), not just the two
# that exist today.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Per-client configuration: TLD, timezone, container uid/gid and anything a
# client adds later. ./setup.sh copies .env.example into .env (repo root) and
# then into every stack that does not have its own copy yet. A stack may ship
# its own .env.example, which is committed too and takes precedence for it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Host networking read by ./host-vlan.sh. Deliberately not part of .env: that
# file is handed to containers, and host interface names have no business in
# there. host.env.example is the committed template.
host.env

# Generated TLS material: leaf certificates, their private keys, the serial
# file and the tls.yml that Traefik's file provider reads.
**/config/certificates/*
**/generate_certificates/root-certificates/
**/generate_certificates/tmp/

# Per-install config, created by ./setup.sh from the committed .example — the
# same deal as .env. Tracked files are ones a `git pull` must be able to
# update; anything an install or its owner edits lives here instead, so a pull
# can never be blocked by a local edit.
**/config/traefik.yml
**/config/unbound/unbound.conf

# Runtime logs, written by containers as root — the default ACL setup.sh puts on
# this directory is what keeps them editable without sudo.
**/config/logs/*

# Dockhand's state, written by the container: .encryption_key, sqlite database,
# icon cache.
**/config/dockhand/*

# Pi-hole's own state: pihole.toml holds the web password and API token, and
# gravity.db is a full copy of the blocklists. The dnsmasq drop-in sitting next
# to it is ours, so it stays tracked.
#
# A stack with more than one service keeps one directory per service —
# {stack}/config/{service}/ — which is what pihole/ and unbound/ are here.
**/config/pihole/*
!**/config/pihole/dnsmasq.d/

# authentik's database and its media (uploaded icons and the like). The
# blueprint next to them is ours and stays tracked.
**/config/postgresql/*
**/config/authentik/data/

# The Dockhand API token ./setup.sh mints for itself and update.sh once
# Dockhand authentication is on.
dockhand/.api-token

# The media tree arr, books and plex share. It is data, not configuration, and
# it can be very large, so none of it belongs in git. ./setup.sh creates the
# empty skeleton (downloads/movies, downloads/tv, ...) so Docker never has to
# invent a root-owned directory here.
downloads/

# *arr stack: each application keeps its database, logs and settings in its own
# config/<service>/ directory.
**/config/bazarr/*
**/config/prowlarr/*
**/config/radarr/*
**/config/sonarr/*
**/config/transmission/*
**/config/cleanuparr/*
**/config/lingarr/*
**/config/lingarr-db/*

# Books: Calibre's library metadata and plugins, CWA's ingest state, Kavita's
# database/covers and Shelfmark's settings and download history. books-glue/glue.py is
# ours and stays tracked, as does the README next to it.
**/config/calibre/*
**/config/calibre-web-automated/*
**/config/shelfmark/*
**/config/kavita/*
**/config/books-glue/*

# Plex's database and media metadata.
**/config/plex/*

# SearXNG: the Valkey dump, the search cache, and settings.yml — per-install
# config created by ./setup.sh from the committed .example, same deal as
# traefik.yml and unbound.conf.
**/config/searxng/cache/*
**/config/searxng/data/*
**/config/searxng/config/settings.yml

# n8n: the workflows/credentials database and the sandbox cluster's mTLS
# material (regenerated on first boot).
**/config/n8n/*
**/config/sandbox-tls/*

# pocket-tts2's model and voice caches, downloaded on first run.
pocket-tts2/config/models/*
pocket-tts2/config/voices/*

# smarthome: Home Assistant's config and database, Mosquitto's data, Zigbee2MQTT,
# ESPHome's device configs and VoiceBM's models and recordings; ESPHome's
# build cache (PlatformIO, several GB, re-downloadable) sits outside config/.
**/config/homeassistant/*
**/config/homeassistant-db/*
**/config/mosquitto/*
**/config/zigbee2mqtt/*
**/config/esphome/*
**/config/voicebm/*
smarthome/cache/

# iptv: threadfin's playlists and buffer, the WARP registration, and
# streams.yaml — per-install, created by ./setup.sh from the committed .example.
**/config/threadfin/*
**/config/warp/*
**/config/streamlink/streams.yaml

# mail, ai: Mailpit's message store, Ollama's keys and its models.
**/config/mailpit/*
**/config/ollama/*
ai/models/

# dsh: the harness runs as a host service, not a container (see dsh/README.md),
# so it keeps no config/ directory. The dsh-mobile checkout that install.sh
# clones is build input, not tracked state — the plugin itself is vendored into
# the DSH profile. dsh/.env is covered by the .env rules above and the rendered
# Traefik route by the config/certificates rule.
dsh/.dsh-mobile/

# Python bytecode from running integrations.py by hand.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
